Has anybody noticed that all the named weapons in the game are melee weapons?
Granted that you can throw some of them, like Mojo, but there aren't any bows,
for example. Now I know we all prefer charging into something with a meaty
weapon as opposed to firing arrows, but it still seems a bit of an imbalance
to me. Hands up anyone who took a sling/bow/crossbow all the way through the
game, powering it up as they went!

Ob. Item idea:
An Aquabus (sp?): A very primitive gun. Often prone to backfire or blow up. If
it hits however (unlikely) it can cause massive damage. Takes a long time to
reload.

PS: Someone mentioned time travel a while back. COOL! We could visit games like
Boss (in the same way that sometimes we visit rogue on dungeon level ~13).
There would be massive potential for culture clash jokes.
